      <div class="pf-why-grid" style="margin-top:2rem;">

        <details class="pf-why-item m-acc"><summary><h3>1930s Semi-Detached</h3></summary><p>The most common Childwall home. Three or four bedrooms. Bay windows, solid build, big gardens. Original pipework was lead and copper. Most has been part-upgraded. Combi boilers were often fitted in awkward spots in the 1990s. We know the layouts.</p></details>

        <details class="pf-why-item m-acc"><summary><h3>1950s Family Semis</h3></summary><p>Built when Childwall grew south after the war. Streets like Score Lane, Welbourne Road and Bowland Avenue. Simpler layouts than the 1930s stock. Standard combi or system boilers. Family bathrooms often updated twice in the last 40 years.</p></details>

        <details class="pf-why-item m-acc"><summary><h3>Large Detached Family Homes</h3></summary><p>Burns Close, Sulgrave Close, Chelwood Avenue. Four and five-bed detached on quiet cul-de-sacs. Two bathrooms or more. Mains pressure unvented cylinders are common. We're G3 qualified for that work.</p></details>

        <details class="pf-why-item m-acc"><summary><h3>Period Homes Near Childwall Abbey</h3></summary><p>The older streets near Childwall Abbey and Childwall Priory Road have some Victorian and 1900s stock. Original features, lead supply pipes still in service in places. We work around period detail with care.</p></details>

        <details class="pf-why-item m-acc"><summary><h3>Modern New Builds and Gated Estates</h3></summary><p>The newer developments around the L16 border. Modern boilers, mains pressure systems, often still under maker warranty. We honour the warranty terms when we work.</p></details>

